==Battleground==
*7 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 7 seconds<sup>210f</sup>, delay 9~13 seconds<sup>270f~390f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 7 seconds<sup>210f</sup>, delay 9~13 seconds<sup>270f~390f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 7~10 seconds<sup>210f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hyppoh]]s spawn after 18 seconds<sup>540f</sup>, delay 15~20 seconds<sup>450f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 18 seconds<sup>540f</sup>, delay 15~20 seconds<sup>450f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Satan Claus]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**10 [[LeMurr]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**10 [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] here are much stronger than the ones in the previous levels, so having all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] is crucial.

Send out 1 [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] to kill the first Ginger Snache. Afterwards, start meatshielding and stack Castaway Cats. Send out any long ranged units you have like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], even better if they're anti-Alien, to deal with the horde of aliens and Satan Claus. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can deal a lot of damage to Satan Claus if he is frozen, but his other forms also work well as general attackers here.

